@title Matchmaking and Game Servers
@subtitle Embergate Online architecture for engineers joining the live team
@author Backend Services
@date 2026-09-22

## Overview

Players are matched into 10-player games and placed on the nearest regional server fleet. Each region can run alone if another region fails.

## Architecture

diagram arch dir=LR title="Matchmaking and game server architecture"
arch: players "Players" user
arch: edge "Global Edge" lb "Routes each player to the closest region"
arch: mm "Matchmaker" svc
arch: alloc "Session Allocator" svc
arch: fleet "Game Server Fleet" svc focus
arch: cache "Regional Cache" cache
arch: profiles "Player Profile Database" db focus
arch: lb "Leaderboard Service" svc focus
arch: players -> edge : connect
arch: edge -> mm : queue request
arch: mm -> cache : skill ratings
arch: mm -> profiles : load profile
arch: mm -> alloc : match of 10 players
arch: alloc -> fleet : start session
arch: players -> fleet : UDP game traffic
arch: fleet -> lb : match results
arch: group region "Regional Stack (same in each of three regions)" mm, alloc, fleet, cache
arch: group shared "Shared across regions" profiles, lb
arch: legend

!! The Player Profile Database and the Leaderboard Service are the only shared parts. They are the ones to watch in a regional failover.

## Regions and capacity

table = Region,Game servers,Matches per server,Concurrent players; us-east,150,6 matches of 10 players,9000; eu-central,150,6 matches of 10 players,9000; ap-southeast,150,6 matches of 10 players,9000

kpi Median matchmaking time | 10 seconds | target
kpi 95th percentile | 30 seconds | target
kpi Max servers per region | 400 | scale up when more than 2000 players wait

Servers scale up to 400 per region when more than 2000 players are waiting in the queue.
